    "narrative": "Andreas Lubitz, the co-pilot of Germanwings Flight 9525, was renowned for his exceptional flying skills and dedication to Lufthansa. With over 4,000 hours of flying time, he was a highly respected member of the aviation community. According to his former instructor at Lufthansa, Andreas Lubitz was a model student and consistently demonstrated superior flying skills. Throughout his career, Andreas Lubitz maintained an impeccable safety record. He had never been involved in any incidents or accidents during his extensive tenure with Lufthansa. The day before the incident, Andreas Lubitz completed a routine flight simulation with perfect scores. This was followed by a successful briefing with the captain, where he displayed exceptional knowledge and preparedness.",
